WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:07.500
Bottom line: standardize reusable skills and MCP integrations, not one universal plugin.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:13.733
Approve a governed portfolio with explicit host compatibility and ownership.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:19.367
Cowork packages skills and connectors in a Microsoft 365 app.

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:24.733
Declarative agents use MCP or REST API actions inside the agent.

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:31.933
GitHub Agent Plugins package portable skills and MCP, plus client-specific components.

00:00:31.933 --> 00:00:36.067
One capability can need three delivery contracts.

00:00:36.633 --> 00:00:42.433
Standardize skill logic and MCP interfaces where compatibility is proven.

00:00:42.433 --> 00:00:49.600
Keep authentication, manifests, discovery and client-only components at the host boundary.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:55.167
REST API actions remain valid; legacy GitHub plugins remain supported.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:59.767
Portability is designed, tested and versioned—not assumed.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:13.433
Approve a small catalog with one product owner per capability, a compatibility matrix, versioned host packages and named service ownership for every MCP server or API.

00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:18.867
Add a route only when demand and controls justify its lifecycle cost.

00:01:18.867 --> 00:01:21.767
Review reuse and exceptions together.
